  "description": "AGSC-01-22: import tolerance has one limit and one record. Derivation, case by case. (1) `newer-minor-imported`: the source declares `spec_version: 1.1.0`, the tool's MAJOR and a newer MINOR. A MINOR only adds (AGSC-00-14) and AGSC-00-21 fixes how a 1.x reader treats what it adds, so the import proceeds: it exits 0, writes the item, and reports the warning AGSC-E506 naming the newer version. (2) `other-major-refused`: the source declares `spec_version: 2.0.0`, a MAJOR this 1.x tool does not implement. Reading another MAJOR is a guess, so the import stops before writing anything, with AGSC-E004; it is exit 2 and not exit 1, because AGSC-09-08 puts invalid configuration in the usage class, and `--dry-run` reports the same thing. (3) `allow-newer-writes`: the same 2.0.0 source with the adapter's own `--allow-newer` flag — an adapter-scoped flag under AGSC-01-26a, which AGSC-09-09 admits — is imported, and the operator, not the tool, has taken the risk. In cases (1) and (3) each written item carries `prov.source_version` and `prov.source_hash`, taken verbatim from the source's published content version and bundle hash, and `prov.origin` stays `imported` as AGSC-01-31 and AGSC-08-01 require. (4) `source-states-neither`: a source that publishes no content version and no bundle hash — a Level-0 publisher, AGSC-06-08a — yields items with both members absent; neither is ever invented.",
